A||||8||3fifty||Subwoofers||||5||
Z||000000||3fifty||02-15-2001||12:35 AM||||I would like to put 2 subs behind the seats in my 85 GT. I have read where some people are cutting the front of the firewall and<BR>recessing the speakers. Has anyone here done<BR>this? How much room is there between the front and rear firewall?Is there a sub that will mount flush to the front firewall once recessed that will not require an additional framework? Thanks for any help.<P>350 one day!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||02-15-2001||01:18 AM||||Fierosound is the man with the idea. There is only about 2 1/2" of space so I would say the answer to being flush with the front is a no. But you'd only lose about an inch with an 8" and about 2" with a 10" sub.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||02-15-2001||01:54 AM||||I'd like to do this someday.. <BR>to any car audio gurus here: how hard would a pair of 8"s behind the seats hit? (techno/trance music is what I listen to mostly.. I love bass)<P>probably with a 600w amp driving them, and a pair of mids in the doors.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000003||Oreif||02-15-2001||10:48 AM||||A pair of 8" subs would pound good in the small cab of the Fiero. I am using 1 8" at 200W. A friend has 1 10" and it pounds good too. It's a matter of preference. 8's will have a sharp punch in the higher bass frequencies where 10's will produce the lower frequencies better. It all depends on if the music has a sharp bass or a "boomy" bass. Usually dance/rap has a boomy type of bass. Simular to what they play at clubs. Then you would want the larger cone size. <BR>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||02-15-2001||11:01 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A>   one 10" in the floor works really well. there are a couple members here with a similar setup and they are happy with it. I sure was! 141.3db! thats jet engine loud! putting them behind the seats will flatten most of the punch due to the seat muffling, similar to systems in a non-extended cab pick-ups. but it'll be better than the weak factory sub. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.kicker.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kicker.com</A>   check out thier L7 series 10" and see is you can cram that behind the seat. one 10" is PLENTY! <BR> <A HREF="http://www.xtant.com" TARGET=_blank>www.xtant.com</A>  - and a nice super low noise amp is a good thing to keep everything running clear and loud. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstxtant.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstxtant.jpg</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||02-16-2001||01:05 AM||||How deep your subwoofers are will determine how deep the boxes will need to be, regardless of whether you cut into the firewall or not.  I've done some more research and have found that some shallow depth subs are now made.  These are high-end high Sound Quality subs.  Be warned, you won't find these on sale at WalMart!!<P>Illusion Audio speakers and subwoofers - subs as shallow as 2.9" <BR><A HREF="http://www.illusionaudio.com/illusion/Driversx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.illusionaudio.com/illusion/Driversx.html</A> <P>Phase Linear S1 10" subs have shallow mounting depth - as low as 3" (80mm)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.phase-linear.com/html/aliante_10si_data.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.phase-linear.com/html/aliante_10si_data.html</A> <P>Morel has very shallow 6" and 8" woofers at 2.5" <BR><A HREF="http://www.morelusa.com/prices/ren.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.morelusa.com/prices/ren.html</A> <P>These come highly recommended by the guys at the <A HREF="http://www.sounddomain.com" TARGET=_blank>www.sounddomain.com</A>  forums..<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 02-16-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||02-16-2001||02:34 AM||||If I could find a 10" that was around 3" deep, and didn't cost several hundred dollars, I'd get a pair of those.<P>I love the club-type music.. not rap though.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||overlord||02-16-2001||09:06 AM||||just my 2 cents.....i had 2 subs behind the seats and didnt like the way they sounded.....plus it was a pain to get the boxes  right (or close enough rather).<P>So i went with 1  10" in footwell  and i am aamazed on how much better  it pounds.  The one 10  apposed to the 2 behind the seats.<BR>Remember the enclosure for the sub is a HUGE factor on sound quality....and i found the footwell to be 10x easier to make||||reg||1
Z||000008||turbo86se||02-16-2001||10:53 AM||||They're not installed yet, but will be before summer, but I've got two 5.25" Bazooka Bass Tubes. They fit perfectly behind the seats. The seat will still go all the way back. I'll probably have a Punch 45 running those. The only bad news is they aren't made anymore, but you can get lucky like me and find them on ebay.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
